{"resourceIdentifier":"1377","resourceName":"Lock Haven Improved Forest Management Project","description":"The Lock Haven Improved Forest Management Project Area (“Project Area”) is a 4,903-acre parcel situated in Clinton County, Pennsylvania. The Project Area has been put under a conservation easement, in perpetuity, with The Nature Conservancy (TNC) with the intention of conserving the property and managing its forest resources sustainably into the future. The Project Area has ecological, scientific, educational and aesthetic value in its present state as a natural area that has not been subject to development or severe resource exploitation. The Project Area is comprised of primarily native forest types characteristic of the region. The forest protects the West Kammerdiner Run and McElhattan Run, headwaters of the Susquehanna River and the Chesapeake Bay. The Project Area contains significant stands of diverse mixed hardwoods as well as oak hickory forest types and wetlands that provide habitat for a multitude of species and natural communities.","location":{"latitude":41.113272,"longitude":-77.418126},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"1377"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"PA"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Lock Haven City Authority"},{"type":"string","value":"Pennsylvania, United States"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"1377"},{"type":"bufferSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"1377"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"6384"}]},{"code":"TOTAL_BUFFER_POOL_CREDITS","values":[{"type":"integer","value":14408}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Agriculture Forestry and Oth